#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:1
msgid "Default Nix expression"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:3
msgid ""
"The source for the [Nix expressions](../../glossary.md#gloss-nix-expression) "
"used by [`nix-env`](../../command-ref/nix-env.md) by default:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:5
msgid "`~/.nix-defexpr`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:6
msgid ""
"`$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/defexpr` if [`use-xdg-base-directories`](../../command-"
"ref/conf-file.md#conf-use-xdg-base-directories) is set to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:8
msgid "It is loaded as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:10
msgid "If the default expression is a file, it is loaded as a Nix expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:11
msgid ""
"If the default expression is a directory containing a `default.nix` file, "
"that `default.nix` file is loaded as a Nix expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:12
msgid ""
"If the default expression is a directory without a `default.nix` file, then "
"its contents (both files and subdirectories) are loaded as Nix expressions. "
"The expressions are combined into a single attribute set, each expression "
"under an attribute with the same name as the original file or subdirectory. "
"Subdirectories without a `default.nix` file are traversed recursively in "
"search of more Nix expressions, but the names of these intermediate "
"directories are not added to the attribute paths of the default Nix "
"expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:16
msgid "Then, the resulting expression is interpreted like this:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:18
msgid ""
"If the expression is an attribute set, it is used as the default Nix "
"expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:19
msgid ""
"If the expression is a function, an empty set is passed as argument and the "
"return value is used as the default Nix expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:21
msgid "**Example**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:23
msgid ""
"If the default expression contains two files, `foo.nix` and `bar.nix`, then "
"the default Nix expression will be equivalent to"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:32
msgid ""
"The file [`manifest.nix`](../../command-ref/files/manifest.nix.md) is always "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:34
msgid ""
"The command [`nix-channel`](../../command-ref/nix-channel.md) places a "
"symlink to the current user's [channels](../../command-ref/files/"
"channels.md) in this directory, the [user channel link](#user-channel-link). "
"This makes all subscribed channels available as attributes in the default "
"expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:37
msgid "User channel link"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:39
msgid ""
"A symlink that ensures that [`nix-env`](../../command-ref/nix-env.md) can "
"find the current user's [channels](../../command-ref/files/channels.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:41
msgid "`~/.nix-defexpr/channels`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:42
msgid ""
"`$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/defexpr/channels` if [`use-xdg-base-directories`](../../"
"command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-use-xdg-base-directories) is set to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:44
msgid "This symlink points to:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:46
msgid "`$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/profiles/channels` for regular users"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:47
msgid "`$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/per-user/root/channels` for `root`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md:49
msgid ""
"In a multi-user installation, you may also have `~/.nix-defexpr/"
"channels_root`, which links to the channels of the root user."
msgstr ""
